Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Offset: the arc join (rounded) joins faces of different offsets with a tube
whose section runs from the one offset to the other, and corners of three
such faces with an ellipsoid (mitcad#2488).

A body offset with offsets of their own on faces (SetOffsetOnFace) and the
arc join: UpdateFaceOffset gave every face a tube or a corner joins to a
face with its own offset that offset too (AddFaces across the edges of the
tubes' type), since the tube was a pipe of one radius and the corner a
sphere. A box shelled outside by 2 mm with its bottom at 5 mm and the
rounded join came out 5 mm all round (MitCad refused it beforehand).

Where the offsets of the two faces of a tube's edge differ, BuildOffsetByArc
now makes the tube with BRepOffset_Offset's new Init (Path, Edge1, Edge2,
Face1, Face2, Offset1, Offset2, ...): its section is the conic from the one
offset to the other, tangent to both offsets (the rational quadratic arc
whose middle pole is where the two tangents meet, weighted as the circle's:
the affine image of the circle of the tube of one offset, that circle where
the offsets are equal). It is exact and the same all along the edge where
the edge is a line along which neither face turns (the section extruded)
or a circle about whose axis both faces turn (the section revolved), one
parameter from Edge1 to Edge2 and the other the path's (u along the
section and v along the path for the extruded section, as the pipe's;
the other way round for the revolved one, whose u is its angle, as a pipe
with ExchangeUV), the face built as the pipe's (initTube, the old Init's body; its new end edges get
their iso-curves as 3d curves, IsoCurve3d). Where the offsets of
the faces round a corner of three faces differ, the corner is the unit
sphere about the vertex stretched along the faces' normals to their
offsets (new Init (Vertex, LEdge, Faces, Offsets)): an ellipsoid through
the tubes' ends and tangent there to the offsets where the three faces are
square to each other, as an exact rational surface; the tubes' end edges
are projected onto it (initCorner, the old Init's body for the sphere).

BRepOffset_Offset::JoinsOffsets(Path, Face1, Face2) and
JoinsOffsets(Vertex, Faces) tell where these can be built.
UpdateFaceOffset (AddFacesJoinedByArc) still gives the faces of a tube's
edge one offset where the tube cannot join different offsets (a curved
edge other than such a circle, a face turning along a straight edge), and
the faces round a corner where it cannot (other than three faces square to
each other), as before; tangential faces as before.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2488.

